      en: "Punta Arenas is a port city in southern Chile, capital of the Magallanes Region, with a population of about 123,000 (2017). Located on the Strait of Magellan, it is the world's southernmost major city. Founded in 1848, it grew due to sheep farming and the gold rush. The climate is cool and windy. Punta Arenas is a gateway for expeditions to Antarctica and Tierra del Fuego. The economy relies on natural gas, sheep farming, and tourism. Landmarks include the cathedral and the regional museum.",
